#tuple
-(item,item2,....)
-sequence of items as a collection
-when we create tuple elements are fixed they cannot be modified it is like list but cannot be modified

#accesing item of a tuple-index
#slicing same as list
-syntax:tuple[start:end:steps] last element will be excluded to print last element use extra index

#to convert list into tuple
-typecasting
l1=[2,3,4]
t1=tuple(l1)

#to convert tuple into list
t1=(1,2,3,"ph")
l1=list(t1)

#Operation of tuple
1.concatenation (+)
2.repetition (*)
3.membership (in,not in)

#count()
-syntax:tuple.count(item)
//same as list but not like string

#index()
-syntax:tuple.index(element)
//to check index of the element

#min()
syntax:min(tuple)

#max()
syntax:max(tuple)

#sum()
syntax:sum(tuple)

#Mutability & Immutability
Mutability-a value that can be changed
eg-List

Immutability-a value that cannot be changed
eg-tuple,string

